# The git mirror's working tree (§16, and GIT_MIRROR_ROOT in §17). It is a git repository of its
# own nested inside this one, and it is not durable state — §17 re-clones it on start. Untracked
# it would be a wall of noise in every `git status`; staged it would become a submodule pointer
# to a commit no clone of this repository can fetch. `src/lib/git/repo.ts` refuses to use a root
# that turns out to be inside another checkout, which is the same hazard caught from the other
# side; this line is what stops the mirror's own files reaching the application's history.
/content/

